.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt PATINA-TILER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-tiler
.Nd the Patina desktop's tiler
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
decides how windows tile on the Patina desktop.
.Xr patina-compositor 1
starts it with the bar and starts it again when it exits, so changing how
windows tile only means installing a new
.Nm
and restarting it from Settings' Processes page; the desktop and its
windows stay.
.Pp
The compositor decides nothing itself: over the session bus it reports
drags and Super with an arrow, and places windows and shows the preview
where it's told.
.Nm
does as Ubuntu does:
.Bl -bullet
.It
A window dragged so the pointer meets the left or right edge of the screen
shows a preview of that half, and dropped there, it takes it.
.It
At the top edge, the window fills the screen: tiled on every side, not
maximised.
The sides win in the top corners.
.It
Super+Left and Super+Right tile the focused window to that half, or restore
it from the other half; Super+Up fills the screen with it, and Super+Down
restores it.
.It
With gaps on (the compositor's
.Ic [gaps] ) ,
the gap goes around the windows and between the halves.
When the work area changes, the halves it tiled are tiled again to fit.
.It
Dragging the line between tiled windows (the compositor's) moves where the
halves meet; the split is kept, and a window tiled to the other side takes
the rest, until no half is tiled any more.
.It
A window opens where its app's window was last, if no other window of its
app is open, or filling the screen if that one closed filling it; one that
would stick out of the screen is moved back inside.
A second window of the same app opens where the compositor puts it.
.It
A window that opens bigger than the screen fills it instead.
.El
.Pp
Only an app's own maximise button maximises a window; that's the
compositor's, not the tiler's.
X11 windows aren't tiled yet.
.Pp
.Nm
holds the bus name
.Sy com.sectorflabs.Patina.Tiler
so another tiler can take it over; while one does,
.Nm
leaves the decisions to it, and decides again once it leaves the bus.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus, where the compositor serves
.Sy com.sectorflabs.Patina.Tiling .
Without it,
.Nm
exits, and windows don't tile.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.local/state/patina-tiler/windows.toml
Where each app's window was last, by app id: written when a window is
dropped somewhere it floats and when it closes.
Deleting the file forgets them.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It runs until the compositor it started with leaves the bus, or another
takes its name.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A tiler of thirds, which takes over while it runs:
.Dl cargo run -p patina-system --example thirds
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-settings 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
